# CC-4 / 13-concurrency.md §23.1: a function cannot return a channel. Phase 39:
# with a `$T` anywhere in the signature tychoc skipped this check and ACCEPTED,
# compiled and RAN the program, while tychoc0 rejected it at the instance -- a
# live accept/reject divergence the same `continue` created. Both compilers now
# reject (differential).
fn f(c: Channel(int), p: $T) -> Channel(int):
    return c

fn main():
    ch := channel(int, 2)
    d := f(ch, 5)
    println("unreachable")
